The same Python 2 problem as 0054, in the pair of scripts that drive the
closure compiler for mojo's JavaScript bindings. js_binary.py is what the build
invokes; compiler.py is the module it imports, and it has the same defect, so
fixing only the first would move the failure one import deeper.

    js_binary.py:126  print args.compiler, ...   ->  print(...)
    js_binary.py:127  print errors               ->  print(errors)
    compiler.py:66    print "(INFO) %s" % msg    ->  print(...)
    compiler.py:74    print >> sys.stderr, ...   ->  print(..., file=sys.stderr)
    compiler.py:313   print stderr               ->  print(stderr)

Worth recording how this was missed. After 0054 the tree was swept for the same
class of defect and the sweep reported zero, which was wrong: it called
py_compile inside a try that also caught the generic Exception and counted that
as a pass, so every SyntaxError that did not arrive wrapped as PyCompileError
was silently treated as success. Redone with ast.parse -- which either returns
or raises SyntaxError, with nothing in between -- the same 752 build-referenced
scripts yield three failures: these two and testing/xvfb.py.

xvfb.py is deliberately left alone. It is the test runner, has fifteen py2
statements rather than five, and nothing content_shell builds invokes it. It is
noted here so the next sweep does not read its absence as an oversight.

--- a/chromium/third_party/closure_compiler/js_binary.py
+++ b/chromium/third_party/closure_compiler/js_binary.py
@@ -123,8 +123,8 @@
 
   returncode, errors = compiler.Compiler().run_jar(args.compiler, compiler_args)
   if returncode != 0:
-    print args.compiler, ' '.join(compiler_args)
-    print errors
+    print(args.compiler, ' '.join(compiler_args))
+    print(errors)
 
   return returncode
 
--- a/chromium/third_party/closure_compiler/compiler.py
+++ b/chromium/third_party/closure_compiler/compiler.py
@@ -63,7 +63,7 @@
       msg: A debug message to log.
     """
